==Critical Damage==
{{Quote|The Damage Total is multiplied by this value when a critical hit is inflicted.<br/>The added Damage is doubled for Big Critical Hits (orange), and tripled for Super Critical Hits (red).|In-game Description}}
===Relative Increases===
Most increases to critical damage are relative '''to the base multiplier'''. Multiple of these stack additively with each other:
:<math>\text{Total Critical Damage Multiplier} = \text{Base Critical Damage Multiplier} \times (1 + \text{Relative Bonus})</math>

:Where the '''Relative Bonus''' is the sum of all applicable bonuses.
:<math>\text{Relative Bonus} = \text{Bonus}_{1} + \text{Bonus}_{2} + \text{Bonus}_{3} + \cdots</math>

As an example, a {{Weapon|Braton}} with {{M|Vital Sense}} and {{M|Bladed Rounds}} has a critical damage multiplier of:
:{{Math|{{text||1.6|hover=Braton's base critical damage multiplier}} {{mul}} (1 + {{M|Vital Sense|120%}} + {{M|Bladed Rounds|120%}})|mt=y}}

===Absolute Increases===
A few effects grant absolute (also called flat) amounts of critical damage which are applied after relative bonuses.

* {{Arcane|Arcane Crepuscular}}
* {{D|Cold}}'s status effect "Freeze"
* {{A|Shroud of Dynar}}
* {{M|Tenacious Bond}}
:<math>\text{Total Critical Damage Multiplier} = \text{Base Critical Damage Multiplier} \times (1 + \text{Relative Bonus}) + \text{Absolute Bonus}</math>

:Where the '''Absolute Bonus''' is the sum of all applicable bonuses.
:<math>\text{Absolute Bonus} = \text{Bonus}_{1} + \text{Bonus}_{2} + \text{Bonus}_{3} + \cdots</math>

As an example, a Braton with {{M|Vital Sense}} (''relative'') and {{M|Tenacious Bond}} (''absolute'') has a critical damage multiplier of:
:{{Math|{{text||1.6|hover=Braton's base critical damage multiplier}} {{mul}} (1 + {{M|Vital Sense|120%}}) + {{M|Tenacious Bond|1.2}}|mt=y}}

===Quantization===
The base critical damage multiplier of a weapon is quantized.<ref>{{Ref|title=Accurate eidolon damage and a convenient spreadsheet comparing weapon builds/rivens|author=BaeckerSkins|year=2022|month=1|day=15|publisher=Reddit|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/Warframe/comments/s4tmbf/accurate_eidolon_damage_and_a_convenient/|access-date=2023-12-03|archive-url=|archive-date=}}</ref><ref>{{Ref|title=Critical multiplier quantization|author=Anon|year=2023|month=12|day=3|publisher=Imgur|url=https://imgur.com/a/jRuWXDq|access-date=2023-12-03|archive-url=|archive-date=}}</ref> This applies before mods, but after certain effects that are additive to the base value. Before encoding, the base critical damage multiplier <math>x</math> is clamped to the range from 0 to 32. The exact 12-bit integer code and decoded multiplier are:

:<math>\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{Code}(x) &= \left\lfloor \operatorname{clamp}(x,0,32) \times \frac{4095}{32} + 0.5 \right\rfloor \\
\text{Quantized Base CDM}(x) &= \operatorname{Code}(x) \times \frac{32}{4095}
\end{aligned}</math>

The 4096 possible codes range from 0 to 4095, so adjacent decoded values differ by <math>32/4095</math>. The calculation uses 32-bit floating-point arithmetic.

As an example, a {{Weapon|Braton}} with {{M|Vital Sense}} excluding quantization for simplicity, has a critical damage multiplier of:
:{{Math|{{text||1.6|hover=Braton's base critical damage multiplier}} {{mul}} (1 + {{M|Vital Sense|120%}})|m=y|mt=y}}

Another similar example, now including quantization, and now with the Incarnon perk Critical Parallel yields a critical damage multiplier of:
:<math>\operatorname{Code}(1.6+0.4) = \left\lfloor 2.0 \times \frac{4095}{32} + 0.5 \right\rfloor = 256</math>
:{{Math|256 {{mul}} (32 / 4095) {{mul}} (1 + {{M|Vital Sense|120%}})|m=y|mt=y}}

